<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Game Mode interventions. Declaring the app a game (android:appCategory="game") lets the
  platform apply these; this file says which are safe for Spiral Knights.

  Downscaling is not: it resizes the backbuffer behind our back, and SK lays its own UI out
  in raw framebuffer pixels. Below roughly 578 px of surface height the client's UI stops
  laying out entirely and character select never appears, the same failure that set the
  0.6 render-scale floor in TouchControlManager. The resolution slider already gives the
  player that trade-off, under a floor we know is safe.

  FPS override is left enabled: we do no frame pacing of our own for it to fight, and
  capping frame rate is a real battery win with no correctness risk.

  supportsBatteryGameMode / supportsPerformanceGameMode are deliberately absent. Setting
  either to true tells the platform the game applies its own per-mode optimisations and
  makes it drop the interventions above; we implement none, so claiming that would trade
  a working default for nothing.
-->
<game-mode-config xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:allowGameDownscaling="false"
    android:allowGameFpsOverride="true" />
